Let us solve the polynomial by first regrouping it
$$x^{1000}=x^{998}\cdot(x^2+1)+x^2-1.$$
From $\quad x^2\equiv -1 \quad$ we have $\quad x^{3}\equiv -x$.
Thus,
$~~x^{2}[:-1]\equiv-x^2-1\equiv1$,
and
$$x^{1000}-2(x^2+1) \equiv 1-2\cdot 1 \equiv -1.$$
Note: the the second equals sign in the above process is
$(-x^2-1)=x^{998}\cdot (x^2+1)-2x^{998}-2$.

